<title>UK: LME copper off highs in PM, spread still buoyant.</title>
<headline>LME copper off highs in PM, spread still buoyant.</headline>
<text>
<p>COPPER - Comes off $2,474 high but spreads remain juicy.</p>
<p>Cash/threes at $100/$110 backwardation, nearly double Wednesday's levels. ZINC - Stronger, but off highs.</p>
<p>ALUMINIUM - Sheds most of gains, slips back to $1,660.</p>
<p>NICKEL - Range-trading, straddles $7,800.</p>
<p>LEAD - Quiet, touch higher. TIN - Slightly firmer.</p>
</text>
